Done. Committed `cb82067` on `sign-panel-compact-bar`.

**Files changed:**

1. **`app/clients/documents/view/[id]/SignPanel.tsx`** — Rewrote from centered 560px card to compact single-row flex bar matching the prototype's `.sign-card` inside `.signed-confirmation`:
   - Removed separate `signature` state; single name input is used for both `name` and `signature` in the POST body
   - Removed visible Date field (auto-populated internally, still sent in body)
   - Layout: left side heading + description, right side flex row with input (200px), "I agree" checkbox, "Sign & submit" button
   - Success state now renders a compact signed-card pill (check icon + "Signed by X on Y") instead of the old large centered card
   - Error banner renders inline below the bar, same compact styling
   - Kept: fetch call, error handling, `docNumber`/`clientName` props, all validation (name + agreed checkbox)

2. **`app/clients/documents/view/[id]/page.tsx`** — Updated the already-signed confirmation block to match the compact signed-card style (`padding: '0 24px 16px'` wrapper, `padding: '10px 16px'`, `borderRadius: 8`, `gap: 8`) for consistency with SignPanel's success state.

**Type-check note:** No `node_modules` installed in this worktree — `npx tsc --noEmit` could not run. The changes are straightforward inline-style-only rewrites of existing React patterns with no new imports or type-sensitive logic.
